{{also|left-over|left over}}

==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|left over}}, {{l|en|left-over}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|left||remaining, abandoned}} + {{m|en|over||excess}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-leftover.wav|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[remaining|Remaining]]; left behind; [[extra]]; [[odd]]; in [[reserve]].
#: {{ux|en|Do you want some of the '''leftover''' supplies from the event?}}
#: {{ux|en|I have some '''leftover''' spaghetti in the fridge, so I don't plan to cook tonight.}}

====Usage notes====
* When used after a verb (as part of a predicate phrase), use two separate words:
*: {{ux|en|I can walk for miles and still have energy [[left over]].}}

